// Title: Potential Discovery Activity Via Dnscmd.EXE
// Sigma ID: b6457d63-d2a2-4e29-859d-4e7affc153d1
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @gott_cyber
// Date: 2022-07-31 | Modified: 2023-02-04
// ATT&CK: discovery, execution
// Description: Detects an attempt to leverage dnscmd.exe to enumerate the DNS zones of a domain. DNS zones used
//   to host the DNS records for a particular domain.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration use
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/dnscmd
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-zones-records
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Dnscmd/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dnscmd_discovery.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\dnscmd.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/enumrecords" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/enumzones" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/ZonePrint" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/info")
